{#
  TOAST — Figma 1490:19024. "Portfolio 2026 is still in progress."

  WHEN IT SHOWS: the first homepage load in a browser tab, and again after a
  hard refresh (⌘⇧R / Ctrl+Shift+R / Ctrl+F5). Not on a normal refresh, and not
  when coming back from a case study. A page cannot tell a hard refresh from a
  normal one, so scripts/v4-toast.js notes the hard-refresh keys as they are
  pressed, and the check below reads that note. The check runs before the toast
  is drawn, so a skipped toast never flashes; a load that shows it starts at
  the top of the page, so the toast never lies over the intro. It is per tab (sessionStorage):
  a new tab or a new visit shows it again.

  Once up, it is gone after 10 seconds: the darker band behind it is the timer,
  filling from left to right, and the toast fades out when it is full
  (_toast.css). The × closes it at once. Hovering or focusing it pauses the
  timer, so it never vanishes while someone is reading it.

  THE RING — 1490:19024. A fuse: the green arc starts full at 0%, and the spark
  at its tip burns it back while the number counts up, stopping at the
  progress value (75%, the arc at 25%) after 2 seconds. The spark keeps
  sparking. scripts/v4-toast.js drives it; the markup holds the end state.
#}
<script>
  try {
    var seen = sessionStorage.getItem("v4-toast-seen");
    var hard = sessionStorage.getItem("v4-hard-reload");
    sessionStorage.removeItem("v4-hard-reload");
    // Back from a case study (/#work-<id>) lands on its card: no toast over it.
    var back = /^#work-/.test(location.hash);
    if ((seen && !hard) || back) document.documentElement.classList.add("is-toast-skipped");
    // Showing it: start at the top. Otherwise the browser restores the last
    // scroll position, which leaves the sticky toast lying over the intro.
    // Coming back to the page restores the reader's place itself
    // (scripts/v4-strip.js), so this costs nothing there.
    else if ("scrollRestoration" in history) history.scrollRestoration = "manual";
    sessionStorage.setItem("v4-toast-seen", "1");
  } catch (e) {}
</script>
<aside class="v4-toast" data-toast aria-label="Site status">
  <div class="v4-toast__body">
    <div class="v4-toast__ring" data-toast-ring data-progress="{{ home.toast.progress }}" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="v4-toast__ring-track" src="/Assets/v4/icons/toast-ring-track.svg" width="40" height="40" alt="" />
      <svg class="v4-toast__ring-arc" viewBox="0 0 40 40"><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="19.17" pathLength="100" /></svg>
      <span class="v4-toast__spark" data-toast-spark>
        <i class="v4-toast__spark-glow"></i>
        <img class="v4-toast__spark-glyph" src="/Assets/v4/icons/toast-spark.svg" width="6" height="6" alt="" />
        <i class="v4-toast__spark-bit"></i><i class="v4-toast__spark-bit"></i><i class="v4-toast__spark-bit"></i>
        <i class="v4-toast__spark-bit"></i><i class="v4-toast__spark-bit"></i><i class="v4-toast__spark-bit"></i>
      </span>
      <span class="v4-toast__ring-value" data-toast-value>{{ home.toast.progress }}%</span>
    </div>
    <div class="v4-toast__text">
      <p class="v4-toast__title">{{ home.toast.title }}</p>
      <p class="v4-toast__detail">{{ home.toast.body }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <button class="v4-toast__close" type="button" data-toast-close aria-label="Dismiss">
    <img src="/Assets/v4/icons/cross.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" />
  </button>
</aside>
